# API Security

## Authentication & Authorization

- Apply auth middleware **globally** — explicitly opt-out for public routes (deny-by-default)
- **Always** verify resource ownership (prevent BOLA/IDOR): check `resource.user_id == current_user.id`
- Verify role/permissions on **every** privileged endpoint — don't rely on frontend hiding UI elements
- **Never** accept and apply all request body fields to models (mass assignment) — use explicit field allowlists

## Input Validation

- Validate **every** request body with schemas (Zod, Pydantic, JSON Schema)
- Validate path params (type, format, range) and query params (sanitize, type-check)
- Verify `Content-Type` header matches expected format
- Set request body size limits: `express.json({ limit: '1mb' })` or equivalent
- Validate file uploads: check MIME type by magic bytes (not extension), enforce size limits, sanitize filenames, store outside webroot

## Rate Limiting (Required)

| Endpoint | Limit |
|----------|-------|
| General API | 100 req/15min per IP |
| Login/auth | 5-10 req/min per IP |
| Registration | 3-5 req/hour per IP |
| Password reset | 3-5 req/hour per email |

- Return `X-RateLimit-Limit`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining`, `X-RateLimit-Reset` headers
- Rate limit by user ID when authenticated, IP as fallback
- Use Redis-backed rate limiting for multi-instance deployments

## Response Security

- **Never** return stack traces, SQL errors, or internal paths in API responses
- Use response DTOs — only return fields the client needs; never return `password`, `internal_id`
- **Always** paginate list endpoints — set max page size (100), default page size (20)
- Remove `X-Powered-By` and `Server` version headers

## GraphQL

- Disable introspection in production: `introspection: process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production'`
- Limit query depth (5-10 levels) and complexity
- Limit batch query count (max 10 per request)
- Add authorization at resolver level, not just query level

## WebSocket

- Authenticate during handshake (token in query or first message)
- Validate `Origin` header during upgrade
- Validate and schema-check all incoming messages
- Rate limit messages per connection (10/second)
- Limit concurrent connections per IP/user

## File Uploads

- Validate MIME type by magic bytes, not extension
- Set size limits (e.g., 5MB)
- **Reject** executable files: `.php`, `.jsp`, `.exe`, `.sh`
- Serve uploads from a **separate** domain/CDN (prevents XSS via uploaded files)
